# BEGIN axiom-graph generated runtime ignores
# Managed by the axiom-skills bootstrap engine. Every rule below is scoped to the
# Axiom namespace (.axiom/): no root-level pattern is added and the whole .axiom/
# directory is never ignored, so human and portable content stays visible to Git.
# Generated live graph output and staging lanes: rebuilt artifacts, never a source.
.axiom/graph/**/live/
.axiom/graph/**/.staging/
# Private native runtime state inside the namespace: the local bindings/state
# pointer, per-worktree hook state and scratch files (not committed, not snapshotted).
.axiom/local/
.axiom/tmp/
# Private native runtime state: SQLite databases and their WAL/SHM/journal sidecars,
# lock and guard files, and atomic temp files. Never committed; never a graph input.
.axiom/**/*.sqlite
.axiom/**/*.sqlite-wal
.axiom/**/*.sqlite-shm
.axiom/**/*.sqlite-journal
.axiom/**/*.sqlite3
.axiom/**/*.sqlite3-wal
.axiom/**/*.sqlite3-shm
.axiom/**/*.sqlite3-journal
.axiom/**/*.lock
.axiom/**/*.guard
.axiom/**/*.tmp
# Ownership boundary (tracked, never matched by this fragment):
#   .axiom/config/solutions/*.json   portable configuration
#   .axiom/annotations/**            human-owned graph inputs
#   .axiom/agent/POLICY.md           managed policy
#   .axiom/agent/POLICY.local.md     human override
#   .axiom/agent/bootstrap.lock.json portable ownership/template hashes
#   .axiom/graph/**/checkpoint/**    optional Git-reviewed snapshots
# A tracked change under .axiom/config/ or .axiom/annotations/ invalidates the
# affected analysis inputs; it is never silently ignored.
# END axiom-graph generated runtime ignores
